/**
 * # Built artifacts and resources
 *
 * Artifacts are intentionally produced or modified material bodies. Resource names
 * their role in activities or plans directed toward goals. This namespace
 * distinguishes the artifact from its use as a resource and places both within
 * the universal BuiltEnvironment domain.
 */
ontology infrastructure
	version 1.0
	using imod, physical, earth
	in domain imod:BuiltEnvironment;
	
/**
 * ## Artifacts as material bodies
 *
 * Artifact records intentional production or modification of a material body.
 * The distinction is useful in ordinary descriptions of built things, while
 * leaving the body's unity and boundaries to its more specific kinds.
 * Artifact is an abstract organizing category; models target suitable concrete
 * specializations.
 *
 * Being an artifact does not establish current usefulness, successful
 * functioning or a Resource role. The producer need not be human, and the
 * meaning is not restricted to Earth. Informational artifacts and constructed
 * cavities are outside this material-body class; a cavity remains distinct
 * from the material structure that bounds it.
 */
@fixme("Same problems as most other things with 'requires identity Goal'")
abstract thing Artifact
    "An intentionally produced or modified material body."
    is physical:MaterialBody
    ;

@fixme("Really not sure of the 'role for goal' thing which seems to be an abuse of the 'for' operator.")
abstract role Resource
     "A resource is the role that objects plays in the context of activities or plans to achieve goals"
     has children
     	@fixme("Do we need these or just the attributes for the nature/provenance of any subject?")
        NaturalResource;